<title>SWEDEN: Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Q4 sales rise 7.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Q4 sales rise 7.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. pharmaceutical group Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn reported these earnings for the fourth quarter of 1996 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>							 1996	   1995</p>
<p>(millions of dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>Earnings/share before</p>
<p> nonrecurring items (cents)			51   vs	48</p>
<p> Earnings/share, fully diluted (cents)	 43   vs	 7</p>
<p> Net earnings before nonrecurring items     268   vs     256</p>
<p> Net earnings					 226   vs	38</p>
<p> Net sales					  1,940   vs   1,805</p>
<p> Operating costs				  1,728   vs   1,773</p>
<p> Other revenue					 44   vs	22</p>
<p> Total operating revenue			1,984   vs   1,827</p>
<p> Operating income				   256   vs	54</p>
<p>For the full-year of 1996, Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn reported the</p>
<p>following. (millions of dollars unless stated)</p>
<p> EPS before nonrecurring items (dollars)	1.90   vs   1.79</p>
<p> EPS fully diluted (dollars)			1.07   vs   1.41</p>
<p> Net earnings before nonrecurring items     998	vs    940</p>
<p> Net earnings					 562	vs    739</p>
<p> Net sales					  7,176	vs  6,949</p>
<p> Operating costs				  6,609	vs  6,080</p>
<p> Other revenue					110	vs    146</p>
<p> Total operating revenue			7,286	vs  7,095</p>
<p> Operating income				   677	vs  1,015</p>
<p> Interest income				    159	vs    216</p>
<p> Interest expense				    56	vs     94</p>
<p> Net earnings					 562	vs    739</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll of 12 analysts showed the market expected the company to post earnings per share (EPS) of $1.92 for 1996 before costs for the merger and for restructuring as well as other one-off items, which together were exepected to amount to $1 a share. Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn has already said that it will pay out a dividend for the fourth quarter of 1996 of $0.27 per share. -- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
